  "article": {
    "hero": {
      "title": "⭐ Pop Star Name Generator",
      "tagline": "Stage names, band names and album titles for the next chart-topper."
    },
    "intro": "Good pop star names sound like a real person with a little extra sparkle, and a few need only one name. This **pop star name generator** makes solo stage names, pop group names and album titles in the shapes real chart acts use.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Eight good pop star names",
        "content": "<p>All eight came from the generator, for solo stars, groups and albums:</p><ul><li><strong>Eden Summers</strong>: a real-sounding name with a bright, seasonal surname.</li><li><strong>Kelsey Starr</strong>: a name with the stardom built in.</li><li><strong>Hollis</strong>: a single name, for a star who doesn't need a surname.</li><li><strong>Marigold</strong>: a one-word name that's also a flower.</li><li><strong>Hattie and the Heartbeats</strong>: a singer and a backing band, an old pop shape.</li><li><strong>Polaroid Hearts</strong>: a group name with a little nostalgia.</li><li><strong>Sad Songs for Happy People</strong>: an album title with a twist in it.</li><li><strong>Champagne for Breakfast</strong>: an album that promises a good time.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Real names, stage names and one-name stars",
        "content": "<p>Pop stars choose their names in three main ways, and the generator makes all three:</p><ul><li><strong>A real-sounding name.</strong> Some stars use their own name (Dua Lipa, Taylor Swift); others change it. Katy Perry was born Katheryn Hudson and took her mother's maiden name to avoid confusion with the actress Kate Hudson. The generator gives names like <em>Summer Vale</em> and <em>Seth Winter</em>.</li><li><strong>One name.</strong> Madonna and Adele use their first names; Rihanna is her middle name. Single names here include <em>Zinnia</em> and <em>Quill</em>.</li><li><strong>A full invention.</strong> Elton John was born Reginald Dwight, and Lady Gaga is Stefani Germanotta. The <a href=\"stage-name-generator.html\">Stage Name Generator</a> is good for names like that.</li></ul><p>Choose <strong>Pop group</strong> for bands like <em>Juno Nash and the Lovers</em>, and <strong>Album</strong> for titles like <em>Half Past Midnight</em>.</p>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Using the names",
        "content": "<ul><li><strong>Say it after \"Ladies and gentlemen…\"</strong> If it sounds right announced, it's a pop name.</li><li><strong>Check it's free</strong> on Spotify, Instagram and TikTok, and check it isn't trademarked if you plan to sell anything with it on.</li><li><strong>Match it to your sound.</strong> A soft single name suits an indie-pop artist; a bright two-word name suits chart pop.</li></ul><p>Starting a group instead? Try the <a href=\"boy-band-name-generator.html\">Boy Band</a>, <a href=\"girl-group-name-generator.html\">Girl Group</a> and <a href=\"kpop-name-generator.html\">K-pop</a> name generators. For the songs, there's the <a href=\"song-title-generator.html\">Song Title Generator</a>.</p><p>For more genres, see all the <a href=\"../categories/music_genres-names.html\">music genre name generators</a>.</p>"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": [
      {
        "question": "How do I come up with a pop star name?",
        "answer": "Start with a name that sounds like a real person, then add a little sparkle: a bright surname (Eden Summers), a single name (Hollis), or a full stage name. Say it out loud as if someone is introducing you on stage."
      },
      {
        "question": "Do pop stars use their real names?",
        "answer": "Some do, like Dua Lipa and Taylor Swift. Others change them: Katy Perry was born Katheryn Hudson, and Elton John was born Reginald Dwight."
      },
      {
        "question": "Can I use these names?",
        "answer": "Yes, they're free to use. Search the name on streaming services and social media first, and check it isn't trademarked if you're building a career on it."
      }
    ]
  }
}
